Architecture
Module breakdown:

Manuscript Loader. Reads and extracts text from the manuscript.

STAG Annotation Loader. Reads and validates STAG annotation files.

Null-Model Protocol Loader. Reads and validates the pipeline specification and the statistical gap results.

Detection Engine. Detects whether the manuscript uses STAG annotations, Null-Model Protocol specifications, or both.

STAG Reporting Standard Checker. Checks the submission against the STAG reporting standard.

Null-Model Protocol Reporting Standard Checker. Checks the submission against the Null-Model Protocol reporting standard.

Required-When-Applicable Resolver. Determines applicability for required-when-applicable items.

Cross-Check Engine. Compares reported numbers with annotation and specification numbers.

Checklist Report Builder. Assembles the checklist report.

Summary Reporter. Produces the summary report.

Reproducibility Recorder. Records the versions, submission identifier, and timestamp.

Web Service Layer. HTTP endpoint.

Command-Line Interface. Argument parsing.

Data flow:

Manuscript, STAG annotations, pipeline specification, and gap results go to the loaders. Detection Engine detects usage. STAG and Null-Model Reporting Standard Checkers run. Required-When-Applicable Resolver determines applicability. Cross-Check Engine compares numbers. Checklist Report Builder assembles. Summary Reporter produces summary. Reproducibility Recorder records.

